{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed use of the basement as self-contained living accommodation and two stairwell access would have a serious and adverse effect on the amenities enjoyed by neighbouring properties, by reason of noise, disturbance and general pedestrian and vehicular activity at and within the vicinity of the site contrary to Local Plan Policy SC7 the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines (2024) and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed basement, due to its size, inclusion of large lightwells, roof lights and staircases and their external appearances, would be an intrusive and incongruous addition to the property, involve unacceptable loss of garden space and diverge from the style of the host property and its neighbours, and the Wellesley Road Conservation Area contrary to Local Plan Policies CC1, CC2 and CC4 and the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines (2024) and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed front boundary treatment and loss of landscaping would be out of keeping with the site and surrounding area and would not therefore preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Wellesley Road Conservation Area contrary to Local Plan Policy CC1, CC2 and CC4, the Council's Residential Extension Guidelines (2024) and the intent of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
